<h2>2. In-Depth Technical Verification Details</h2>

<h3>Issue 2: Noble Username Color Consistency</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Apply the currently active Noble tier's approved username styling consistently across Party Room mic nickname, full profile, room mini profile, room chat, and room entry banner without SVIP override.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
Implementation: NobleBadgeHelper.buildStyledUsername()<br>
File: mobile app/lib/core/utils/noble_badge_helper.dart (Lines 341-368)
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Viscount:</strong> Blue (<code>#2196F3</code>)</li>
  <li><strong>King:</strong> Yellow / Golden (<code>#FFD700</code>)</li>
  <li><strong>Marquis / Mercurius:</strong> Red (<code>#E53935</code>)</li>
  <li><strong>Imperial (Emperor):</strong> Multi-stop animated linear gradient shader (<code>#29B6F6</code> Royal Blue, <code>#FFD54F</code> Imperial Gold, <code>#4FC3F7</code> Cyan, <code>#FFE082</code> Gold) rotating continuously via <code>AnimatedImperialUsername</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>5 Surfaces Wired:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li>Party Room Mic Nickname: <code>multi_role_seat_grid.dart:491</code></li>
      <li>Full Profile: <code>profile_screen.dart:426</code> and <code>user_profile_details_screen.dart:1947</code></li>
      <li>Room Mini Profile: <code>in_room_profile_card_sheet.dart:355</code></li>
      <li>Room Chat Username: <code>animated_live_comment_item.dart:360</code></li>
      <li>Room Entry Banner: <code>svip_entry_banner.dart:217</code> and <code>tiktok_user_join_banner.dart:299</code></li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 7: Gender Badge Discrepancy</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Eliminate mismatch where the same account showed blue in full profile and pink in room mini profile.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
Full Profile: mobile app/lib/features/profile/user_profile_details_screen.dart (Lines 1973-1987)<br>
Room Mini Profile: mobile app/lib/features/party_room/widgets/in_room_profile_card_sheet.dart (Lines 368-397)
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Both views now evaluate <code>user.gender.toLowerCase() == 'female'</code>:
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Female:</strong> Pink Accent (<code>#E91E63</code>) with <code>Icons.female_rounded</code></li>
      <li><strong>Male:</strong> Blue Accent (<code>#3897F0</code>) with <code>Icons.male_rounded</code></li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>The room mini profile invokes <code>_loadAuthoritativeUser()</code> on sheet initialization to hydrate the true authoritative account gender rather than relying on unpopulated room participant payloads.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 4 + 5: Daily Check-In & Game Quest Eligibility</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Prevent generic network error on Day 1 claim and decouple mini game quest completion from gift sending.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
File: mobile app/lib/features/rewards/rewards_screen.dart (Lines 32-35, 71-122, 482-530)
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><code>_claimCheckin()</code> submits <code>POST /v1/users/me/daily-checkin/claim</code>, updates wallet coins upon server confirmation, and marks the day claimed.</li>
  <li>Catches 400/409 duplicate claim codes safely and reconciles state without blocking the user.</li>
  <li><code>_gameTaskCompleted</code> and <code>_giftTaskCompleted</code> are completely separate variables in state. Gifting gifts does not set <code>_gameTaskCompleted</code> to true.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 11: Wealth Level Progression Schedule</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Replace the fixed 10,000 coins per level formula with the approved 100-level cumulative sending schedule dated 3 November 2026.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
File: mobile app/lib/core/utils/wealth_level_helper.dart (Lines 52-212)<br>
UI: mobile app/lib/features/profile/level_center_screen.dart (Lines 86-97)
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Maximum level is exactly 100 at 250,000,000 cumulative sending coins.</li>
  <li>Level 1: 0 coins. Level 2: +10,000 (10K total). Level 3: +20,000 (30K total). Level 4: +40,000 (70K total).</li>
  <li>Single large gifts can cross multiple thresholds; extra progress toward the next level is preserved.</li>
  <li>Level 100 displays "MAX LEVEL" with no Level 101 overflow.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 14: Room Sending Total Persistence on Reopening</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Ensure daily trophy/sending total does not reset to zero when an Audio Party room is closed and reopened.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
Files: mobile app/lib/providers/live_party_provider.dart & mobile app/lib/core/utils/room_config_manager.dart
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><code>RoomConfigManager.instance.saveRoomSendingTotal(roomId, total)</code> caches the sending total locally.</li>
  <li>On room join/wake-up, the total is restored immediately from cache and synchronized against <code>GET /v1/rooms/:id/rankings?period=daily</code>.</li>
  <li>Leaving the room or closing the room does not clear the saved total for that room ID.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 18: Permanent Party Room Sleep & Wake Lifecycle</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> When host leaves and room is empty for 10-12 seconds, room enters sleep mode. Wakes up when host or user enters.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
Files: mobile app/lib/features/party_room/create_party_screen.dart & live_party_room_screen.dart
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Host exit in <code>live_party_room_screen.dart</code> vacates Seat 0 and disconnects Agora without calling room termination.</li>
  <li>When entering via <code>create_party_screen.dart</code>, the backend returns the sleeping room via <code>getMyPartyRoom()</code>.</li>
  <li>Tapping <strong>"Open My Room"</strong> executes <code>POST /v1/rooms/:id/join</code> which wakes the room to <code>LIVE</code> in database and broadcasts <code>room:woke_up</code>.</li>
  <li><em>Audit Note on Creation:</em> If user clicks "Cancel" on the dialog, line 336 hits <code>return;</code> which prevents creating a fresh party room. Recommendation provided to offer "End Old & Create New" similar to Live Video broadcast.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 23: Merchant Role Visibility in App Profile</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Show Merchant Center in profile menu when authorized on the user account, distinct from Coin Seller.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
Files: mobile app/lib/features/profile/profile_screen.dart (Lines 775-778, 889-895) & mobile app/lib/models/user_model.dart
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><code>UserModel.fromJson</code> parses active merchant authorization from <code>isMerchant</code>, <code>hasMerchantPortal</code>, <code>userType == 'MERCHANT'</code>, and <code>role == 'merchant'</code>.</li>
  <li><code>profile_screen.dart</code> displays "Merchant Center" with badge "MERCHANT" linking to <code>MerchantCenterScreen()</code>.</li>
  <li>If Coin Seller is also active, both entries appear side-by-side with distinct labels and destinations.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 24, 25 & 26: Admin Web Panel Dependencies</h3>
<p><strong>Audit Finding:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Issue 24 (BD Verification Crash):</strong> The error <code>TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'id')</code> occurs in the Admin Web React/Vue frontend during BD registration lookup. The mobile Flutter app already has <code>BD Center</code> fully wired and placed above Host Center in <code>profile_screen.dart:847-853</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Issue 25 (Push Notification Broadcast):</strong> The unresponsive "Broadcast Now" button belongs to the Admin Web dashboard push form. Mobile client push handling is functional via <code>NotificationProvider</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Issue 26 (VIP Noble 7 Tiers Limit):</strong> The dropdown listing extra tiers belongs to the Admin Web panel. The mobile app strictly defines and uses the 7 approved Noble tiers in <code>noble_badge_helper.dart</code> and <code>aristocracy_center_screen.dart</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 27: Global Rankings Parity</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Verify app leaderboard categories and periods against admin requirements.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
File: mobile app/lib/features/leaderboard/leaderboard_screen.dart (Lines 74-75, 120-150)
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Categories: <code>['Room', 'Wealth', 'Charm', 'CP', 'SVIP']</code></li>
  <li>Periods: <code>['Daily', 'Weekly', 'Monthly']</code></li>
  <li>Fetches authoritative rankings from <code>/v1/rankings</code> and excludes test seed accounts. Mobile frontend is 100% compliant with product specifications.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Issue 29: Animated King Noble Badge</h3>
<p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Use the designated winged golden crest with crown, jewels, and central sword in Profile Medal section and Aristocracy King preview.</p>
<div class='code-box'>
Files: mobile app/lib/features/aristocracy/aristocracy_center_screen.dart (Lines 144-151, 776-781) & mobile app/lib/core/utils/noble_badge_helper.dart (Line 41)
</div>
<p><strong>Verification Details:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Configured with <code>assets/nobles/ZP-037_tier-6-king_badge.webp</code> / <code>ZP-034_tier-6-king_badge.webp</code>.</li>
  <li>Renders the exact authorized animated golden winged sword crest with high-fidelity detail and no generic placeholder.</li>
</ul>

